Hello all,

I am trying to extract sleep measures from UK BioBank raw accelerometer
data (AX3) using GGIR package (v2.1-0). I came across couple of papers and also
some posts in this group, in which it is recommended to first convert .cwa files
to .wav files using omconvert. I was wondering if anyone could advise what’s
the reason behind this? As far as I looked into GGIR guideline, it can resample
and auto-calibrate the input raw signal.

Also, I am new to sleep research and using the following
script for analysing the AX3 data. I was wondering if anyone has any suggestions/experience
for parameter setup on this dataset? Any input would be highly appreciated.

 g.shell.GGIR(#-------------------------------

# General parameters

#-------------------------------

mode=c(1,2,3,4,5)

datadir = "/UKBB/Raw_Data/",

outputdir = “/UKBB/GGIR_output/”,

overwrite = FALSE,

do.parallel = T,

chunksize = 1,

idloc=2,

storefolderstructure = FALSE,

print.filename=TRUE,

#=====================

          # Part 1

#=====================

printsummary=TRUE,

#=====================

# Part 2

#=====================

strategy = 1,

hrs.del.start = 0,
hrs.del.end = 0,

maxdur =
9,
includedaycrit = 16,

qwindow=c(0,24),

mvpathreshold =c(100),

bout.metric = 4,

excludefirstlast = FALSE,

includenightcrit = 16,

#=====================

# Part 3 + 4

#=====================

def.noc.sleep = 1,

outliers.only = FALSE,

criterror = 4,

do.visual = TRUE,

#=====================

# Part 5

#=====================

threshold.lig = c(30), threshold.mod = c(100),  threshold.vig = c(400),

boutcriter = 0.8,      boutcriter.in <http://boutcriter.in> =
0.9,     boutcriter.lig = 0.8,

boutcriter.mvpa = 0.8, boutdur.in <http://boutdur.in> = c(1,10,30), boutdur.lig = c(1,10),

boutdur.mvpa = c(1),

includedaycrit.part5 = 2/3,

timewindow = c("WW"),

#=====================

# Report generation

#=====================

#do.report=c(2, 3, 4, 5),

dofirstpage = TRUE,

visualreport=TRUE)

Kind regards,

Mahnoosh

